{
    "background_story": "In ancient Mesopotamian mythology, Jase was a demigod born to a mortal father and the goddess Sarpanitu, patron deity of fertility and war. As the son of a powerful goddess, Jase inherited her fierce warrior spirit and unwavering dedication to justice. He roamed the land, fighting against evil forces that threatened the balance of nature and human societies. With his mother's blessing, Jase wielded the power to control the cycles of nature, summoning the fury of storms and the nourishing rains. His legendary exploits earned him the respect and admiration of gods and mortals alike. Though his name was whispered in awe, Jase remained humble, knowing that his true strength came from his mother's divine legacy and his own unshakeable commitment to protecting the innocent.",
